While executing this code we are getting NullReferenceException on Serialize with latest Protobuf V2. But it works fine with V1.
Worst part of the NullReferneceException behavior is, for a large DTO we wont be able to figure out which type/collection is having null value. We have tried this solution https://code.google.com/p/protobuf-net/issues/detail?id=217. 
But can we have the earlier version behavior than throwing NullReferenceException. Could you please tell us why you people removed the old behavior? 

For null values on reference types, Protobuf V2 is creating default instance with default values. But in earlier version it was just neglecting null values.
Please find the scenario below.

```
class Program
{
    [ProtoContract]        
    public abstract class NullableBase
    {
        public NullableBase()
        {
        }

        [ProtoMember(1)]
        public int? Value { get; set; }            
    }

    [ProtoContract]
    public class NullableChild:NullableBase
    {
        [ProtoMember(2)]
        public string StrValue { get; set; }
    }

