Serialization is simple - just cast to `IMessage` (if you can't constrain it otherwise) and then you've got the `ToByteArray` extension method:

``` csharp
byte[] data = ((IMessage) input).ToByteArray();
```

The reverse is trickier, because we need to get at a parser. In `JsonParser` I rely on there being a parameterless constructor for generated message types - and you can too:

``` csharp
public static T ReadMessage<T>(Stream stream) where T : IMessage, new()
{
    T message = new T();
    message.MergeFrom(stream);
    return message;
}
```

Is that the sort of thing you're thinking of?

