Hi!

Can I create pull request with changing block_alloc and block_dealloc to custom allocator class?

It's need for parse heterogeneous protobufs in loop. For example:

(hereinafter, the pseudo-code)

```
message Test {
  repeated A a = 1;
  repeated B b = 2;
  repeated C c = 3;
}
```

Test messages lies in a row in file. I mean something like this:

```
while (true) {
  int32_t x = 0;
  read(fd, &x, sizeof(x));

  buffer.resize(x);
  read(fd, buffer.data(), buffer.size());

  Test test;
  test.ParseFromArray(buffer.data(), buffer.size());

  // Process test.
}
```

It will be so slow. Of course I can do something like this:

```
Test test;

while (true) {
  int32_t x = 0;
  read(fd, &x, sizeof(x));

  buffer.resize(x);
  read(fd, buffer.data(), buffer.size());

  test.ParseFromArray(buffer.data(), buffer.size());

  // Process test.
}
```

It will be much faster, but memory using will be awful. I can use Arena:

```
Arena arena;

while (true) {
  int32_t x = 0;
  read(fd, &x, sizeof(x));

  buffer.resize(x);
  read(fd, buffer.data(), buffer.size());

  Test* test = Arena::CreateMessage<Test>(&arena);
  test.ParseFromArray(buffer.data(), buffer.size());

  // Process test.

  arena.Reset();
}
```

Getting better, but still relatively slowly.

I can override block_alloc and block_dealloc, but it's not provide sufficient flexibility.

But if I will use custom pool allocator, I can get much better performance.

```
PoolAllocator allocator;
allocator.PreallocateBuffer(8_gb)

ArenaOptions options.
options.allocator = &allocator.

Arena arena(options);

while (true) {
  int32_t x = 0;
  read(fd, &x, sizeof(x));

  buffer.resize(x);
  read(fd, buffer.data(), buffer.size());

  Test* test = Arena::CreateMessage<Test>(&arena);
  test.ParseFromArray(buffer.data(), buffer.size());

  // Process test.

  arena.Reset();
}
```

P.S. It's real use of protocol buffers in openstreetmap pbf data parsing.

