We have a problem attempting to use the framework support in the ObjectiveC compiler. The issue is two-fold:
1. Local proto dependencies within the same framework use "path/to/The.pbobjc.h" dependencies, but the framework imports expect them to be flattened as <framework/The.pbobjc.h> (or paths to be searched recursively).
2. We may have multiple protos with the same name in the same module under different folder paths, which will conflict on being flattened. e.g. squareup/group1/Options.pbobjc.h & squareup/group2/Options.pbobjc.h (no naming conflict by having a unique prefix)

For this reason, I believe we should be maintaining the folder structure within the frameworks and the imports that are added should continue to use the explicit full path to the dependency. I believe the fix would look like:

```
diff --git a/src/google/protobuf/compiler/objectivec/objectivec_file.cc b/src/google/protobuf/compiler/objectivec/objectivec_file.cc
index cf8c34e..421d4e1 100644
--- a/src/google/protobuf/compiler/objectivec/objectivec_file.cc
+++ b/src/google/protobuf/compiler/objectivec/objectivec_file.cc
@@ -110,14 +110,14 @@ void ImportWriter::AddFile(const FileGenerator* file) {
   if (proto_lookup != proto_file_to_framework_name_.end()) {
     other_framework_imports_.push_back(
         proto_lookup->second + "/" +
-        FilePathBasename(file_descriptor) + extension);
+        file->Path() + extension);
     return;
   }

   if (!options_.generate_for_named_framework.empty()) {
     other_framework_imports_.push_back(
         options_.generate_for_named_framework + "/" +
-        FilePathBasename(file_descriptor) + extension);
+        file->Path() + extension);
     return;
   }

```

This leads to imports looking like:

```
#import <Framework/path/to/The.pbobjc.h>
```

I'm not sure if there is something I'm missing though. I'd be happy to open a PR with this change if this is an agreeable solution. Thanks for your feedback.

