@kentonv the problem arises when an older client is trying to verify the hash of a proto containing extension fields it doesn't understand. With these tweaks, the verifier wouldn't need the new schema to verify the proto.

The serializer would in all conceivable cases (at least for our purposes) have the schema, so it would know the appropriate bits to flip when serializing.

All that said, this probably wouldn't work (or would be rather inconvenient) with gRPC, since we'd need to flip those bits back prior to gRPC parsing the messages, and that would probably involve shoving them in byte fields and parsing them manually for every RPC. Blargh :cry:

First off, `mypy-protobuf` is great. Getting it integrated into the main project here would be awesome.

That said, if you are using a recent Python version (3.7+) and willing to try another plugin I've built https://github.com/danielgtaylor/python-betterproto which generates dataclasses with proper types among other improvements. For example, given this input:

```protobuf
syntax = "proto3";

package repeatedmessage;

message Test {
  repeated Sub greetings = 1;
}

message Sub {
  string greeting = 1;
}
