@mayamoon, in proto source, to refer to the timestamp, you have to use the package and type as defined in the proto file, not as you would use them in C Sharp source.

In the proto file, the "google/protobuf/timestamp.proto" file declares the package as "google.protobuf" *not* "Google.Protobuf.WellKnownTypes".

So replace your `Packet` message with this:

```proto
message Packet {
   int64 id = 1;
   Message payload = 3;
   google.protobuf.Timestamp times = 4;
}
```

