I tried your sample code and found that the NullPointerException is actually because of the bDescriptor being null, i.e., you haven't actually gotten the right extension descriptor. To get the descriptor for the extension, you need to do this instead:

```java
FieldDescriptor bDescriptor = B.getDescriptor().getExtensions().get(0);
```

You need to get it from `B` because the extension is defined in the scope of `B`.

After that you will still get an exception if you try to call getFieldBuilder() on the descriptor. That's because field builder is not supported for extensions. You will instead need to do it like this:

```java
FieldDescriptor bDescriptor = B.getDescriptor().getExtensions().get(0);
Builder subBuilder = ((Message) builder.getField(bDescriptor)).toBuilder();
...  // use subBuilder
builder.setField(bDescriptor, subBuilder.build());
```

