@mishas, FWIW, `google.protobuf.BytesValue` does already exist, but it is in `google/protobuf/wrappers.proto`.

Sadly, the `google/protobuf/struct.proto` file really should be renamed `google/protobuf/json.proto` because it purely for translating JSON to proto. A `google.protobuf.Value` is a JS value, which is why the options are so limited and do not match proto's own scalar types (not even distinguishing between floating-point and integer values, 32-bit and 64-bit, or signed and unsigned integer types).

To fully represent an arbitrary protobuf message using a generic "struct" message, you'd need to create your own `Value`, `ListValue`, and `Struct` instead of using these well-known types.

