Sorry, but I don't think we want an option to change the behavior of unknown fields for proto2. I also believe that won't solve your problem because unknown fields are not the only thing that get allocated in parsing. For example, parsing a string field will also call malloc. Same goes for any repeated fields, message fields etc.

In your case, I think using the arena feature might be your best bet. It basically allows you to specify a buffer ahead of time and the parsing code will grab memory chunks from the buffer without calling malloc. It gives you better control over memory allocations.  For example:

```cpp
{
  ArenaOptions options;
  // Tell arena to use an existing buffer.
  options.initial_block = some_existing_buffer;
  options.initial_block_size = buffer_size;
  Arena arena(options);
  // Create a Foo proto on the arena.
  Foo* foo = Arena::CreateMessage<Foo>(&arena);
  // Use Foo like a regular proto message.
  foo->ParseFromString(input);
  // No need to delete foo
}
```

