  INV = 0;
  reserved 3 to 5;
  reserved 5 to 10;
}
```

It should complain that the two ranges overlap (which is how message reserved ranges work).

And it turns out that it is *trying* to validate overlaps but does so as if the range were open. Example:

```proto
syntax = "proto3";

enum V {
  INV = 0;
  reserved 3 to 5;
  reserved 4 to 10;
}
```

Error message:
```
test.proto: Reserved range 4 to 9 overlaps with already-defined range 3 to 4.
```

