Protobuf can only be parsed if the type is known by the receiver. If you send different types of protos over the wire, you must accompany the data with some identification information so the receiver can tell what proto type it has received. The commonly used techniques are:
1. Embed the type name in a header with proto serialized bytes as the payload. RPCs generally take this approach, although they usually encode the rpc method name instead of proto type name, but the type name can be inferred from the method name.
2. Use one single proto type on the wire and put everything you want in this one single type. For example, you can declare a message with an oneof:
```proto
message Request {
  oneof oneof_request {
    SearchRequest search = 1;
    ChatRequest chat = 2;
    // ...
  }
}
```

