@acozzette reading #3625, there seems there's an issue with protobuf's internal representation of enums, as enum names are global in the scope of protobuf's internal scope (not cpp symbol scope).

Obviously code would be broken, since the generated enums are `enum`s and not `enum class`es, meaning that they must have been used as such.

