@xfxyjwf Well, there is a misunderstanding, however, I think it's different: proto types exist on a much higher level of the parser then where merging happens.  So, there's nothing to stop you from merging chunks of data that would have mapped to different C++ types before you interpret them as such.

What I'm saying is that this ability is not just not very useful, is that it is also dangerous, and it's danger haven't been discovered because, mostly people using Protobuf don't even realize it is possible to use it like that.

I am convinced that dropping this feature in the next version in favor of packed length-delimited fields would've made everyone happier: you get more compact wire format, you get an ability to generate pull/push parsers, you have a more uniform binary parser and all you have to pay for this is an ability to merge messages.  Seems like a huge win to me.

