Hello,

I'm trying to dynamically get a `oneof` type.  Let's assume we have AWS resources, and I have them wrapped in another protobuf:

```
message WrappedResource {
  oneof resource {
    Ec2Instance ec2_instance = 1;
    SecurityGroup security_group = 15;
  }
  ... other fields ...
}

message Ec2Instance {
  ... fields ...
}

message SecurityGroup {
  ... fields ...
}
```

When I am trying to get whichever resource is inside the `WrappedResource` message I can do so if I know what type of message it is: `wrappedResource.getEc2Instance()` or `wrappedResource.getSecurityGroup`, however if I don't know (nor do I specifically care in the specific function I'm implementing) how do I obtain the `resource` object?

The closest I've been able to come up with is `wrappedResource.wrappers_[wrappedResource.getResourceCase()]`, however I don't really feel comfortable using protobuf internals to achieve this.  Is there a better way to indiscriminately get whichever resource is contained within the outside message natively?

Right now we are manually mapping the resource types to the individual functions, but as the system scales this will quickly become untenable, so any insight would be great!

Thanks in advance!
Kirk

nodes.body:
The recommended way to access oneof is to switch on the oneof case. Something like:
```
switch (wrappedResource.getResourceCase()) {
  case ResourceCase.EC2_INSTANCE: ...;
  case ResourceCase.SECURITY_GROUP: ...;
}
```

I'm not sure about Javascript, but in most languages, the compiler can check whether you have exhausted all the cases and enforce all cases are handled when new field is added to the oneof.

