I haven't had a chance to dig into why this is happening yet, but for what it's worth I had encountered some similarly odd behavior as I was writing my own minimal base64 encoder/decoder. The cause for my problem had been that during the creation of the 24-bit intermediate pattern (3 octets/4 encoded characters), I had been assuming that there were 8 bits in each of the values that were being bitwise or'd together, but there were not and some bits were being overwritten. I fixed it by casting them to unsigned chars before or'ing.

