[#3194](https://github.com/google/protobuf/issues/3194)
***Current Behaviour*** : JsonFormat serializes int64 as strings.  
***Reason*** : It's because int64 is not a standard JSON type and many JSON parsers don't support int64 precision.   
***Expected Behaviour*** : By default, JsonFormat should serialize int64 as strings to be compatible. But an additional flag should be added to printer to print as integer.
***Use case*** : If a parser which is expecting a long will break at string.

**Describe the solution you'd like**
Add a new flag _serialize64AsIs_ (or a better name).
<pre><code>
        case INT64:
        case SINT64:
        case SFIXED64:
          if (serialize64AsIs) {
            generator.print("\"");
          }
          generator.print(((Long) value).toString());
          if (serialize64AsIs) {
            generator.print("\"");
          }
          break;</pre></code>

