I found this comment: https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/blob/47d33e752e5256bec315e5867b940ca33d66e8a2/csharp/src/Google.Protobuf/Reflection/MessageDescriptor.cs#L171

```
        /// For wrapper types (<see cref="Google.Protobuf.WellKnownTypes.StringValue"/> and the like), the parser returned here
        /// will be the generated message type, not the native type used by reflection for fields of those types. Code
        /// using reflection should call <see cref="IsWrapperType"/> to determine whether a message descriptor represents
        /// a wrapper type, and handle the result appropriately.
```

however the `IsWrapperType` method is marked internal:

```
        internal bool IsWrapperType => File.Package == "google.protobuf" && File.Name == "google/protobuf/wrappers.proto";
```

I wonder if part of the fix here would be to make `IsWrapperType` public. Then maybe just a utility method somewhere `ToWrappedType` that would convert a `bool` to a `BoolValue` and so on? I implemented my own for these, but perhaps others would find them useful.

