In the `protobuf.so` PHP extension, when using the correct namespaces for sub-messages, a warning is thrown. Steps to reproduce:

1. Install a library with sub-messages. E.g. `google/common-protos`:
     ```
     composer require google/common-protos
    ```

2. Create a sub-message using a properly namespaced submessage classname:
    ```php
    require_once __DIR__ . '/vendor/autoload.php';

    // set a custom error handler so that the deprecated warnings are no longer suppressed
    set_error_handler(function ($errno, $errstr) {
        // Keep existing error handling
        printf("%s: %s\n", $errno, $errstr);
    }, E_ALL);

    // This should NOT result in a warning (but it does when the extension is enabled)
    $link = new Google\Rpc\Help\Link;
    ```

The output is the following:

```
16384: Google\Rpc\Help_Link is deprecated and will be removed in the next major release. Use Google\Rpc\Help\Link instead
16384: Google\Rpc\QuotaFailure_Violation is deprecated and will be removed in the next major release. Use Google\Rpc\QuotaFailure\Violation instead
16384: Google\Rpc\PreconditionFailure_Violation is deprecated and will be removed in the next major release. Use Google\Rpc\PreconditionFailure\Violation instead
16384: Google\Rpc\BadRequest_FieldViolation is deprecated and will be removed in the next major release. Use Google\Rpc\BadRequest\FieldViolation instead
```

The output _should_ be nothing, since the proper namespaced class name is used.

Similarly, if the wrong name is used, the output should print a single deprecated warning:

```php
require_once __DIR__ . '/vendor/autoload.php';

// set a custom error handler so that the deprecated warnings are no longer suppressed
set_error_handler(function ($errno, $errstr) {
    // Keep existing error handling
    printf("%s: %s\n", $errno, $errstr);
}, E_ALL);

// This SHOULD result in a warning, and it does when the extension is enabled, but additional errors are printed as well.
$link = new Google\Rpc\Help_Link;
```

Without the extension enabled:
```
16384: Google\Rpc\Help_Link is deprecated and will be removed in the next major release. Use Google\Rpc\Help\Link instead
```

With the extension  enabled:

```
16384: Google\Rpc\Help_Link is deprecated and will be removed in the next major release. Use Google\Rpc\Help\Link instead
16384: Google\Rpc\QuotaFailure_Violation is deprecated and will be removed in the next major release. Use Google\Rpc\QuotaFailure\Violation instead
16384: Google\Rpc\PreconditionFailure_Violation is deprecated and will be removed in the next major release. Use Google\Rpc\PreconditionFailure\Violation instead
16384: Google\Rpc\BadRequest_FieldViolation is deprecated and will be removed in the next major release. Use Google\Rpc\BadRequest\FieldViolation instead
```

With the extension enabled, additional irrelevant class name warnings are produced. Both of these are resulting from the same problem, so there's really only one core problem in the extension - ensure the deprecated warning is only thrown when the deprecated sub-message class names are requested.

Related to https://github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-php/issues/1588

