**What did you do?**
Noticed one anomaly in the PHP protobuf generated classes. It seems like the generated classes maintains the same order of the fields as they are declared inside the message for PHP as compared to the sorted order (based on the "tag") generated for other languages like Java. 

_**This leads to serialization differences with generated classes for other languages like Java and C#.**_

For example
```
message Example {
  required int32 f = 2;
  required sting ff = 1;
}
```

**What did you expect to see**
```
class Example {
  private $ff = '';
  private f;
}
```
In Java and C# it is generated in this order.

**What did you see instead?**
```
class Example {
   private $f;
   private $ff = '';
}
```
In Php it is generated in above way.

