That option was a mistake, since end users like you can do it better than the compiler can and it should probably be removed (@jtattermusch can we do this, it's undocumented and was never in any release notes).

If you need `Serializable` support in a message, you can implement it manually via a partial class definition like so:

For `foo.proto`
```proto
syntax = "proto3";

message Foo {
    int64 id = 1;
    int32 value = 2;
}
```
In another `.cs` file
```cs
[Serializable]
public partial sealed class Foo : ISerializable
{
    public Foo(SerializationInfo info, StreamingContext context)
    {
        Id = (long)info.GetValue(nameof(Id), typeof(long));
        Value = (int)info.GetValue(nameof(Value), typeof(int));
    }
    public void GetObjectData(SerializationInfo info, StreamingContext context)
    {
        info.AddValue(nameof(Id), Id);
        info.AddValue(nameof(Value), Value);
    }
}

