I will describe the solution here. If you encounter the same problem, you can learn from it.

Solutions:
I serialized it with the method `serializeToString()`, and then converted the string to bytes as I output the data. Other languages can deserialize it directly with protobuf.

Custom function:

```

/**
 * Convert a String String to bytes
 * @param $string               The string to convert
 * @param string $sep           The separator
 * @param bool $return_string   Whether string：true string、false An array of
 * @return string|array         “11 25  57 45 48 51 45 50”
 */
function strToBytes($string, $sep = ' ', $return_string = true)
{
    $bytes_array = array();
    for ($i = 0; $i < strlen($string); $i++) {
        $bytes_array[] = ord($string[$i]);
    }
    $bytes = $bytes_array;
    if ($return_string == true) {
        $bytes = implode($sep, $bytes_array);
    }
    return $bytes;
}
/**
 * Byte array to string
 * @param string|array $bytes       Bytes to convert：“11 25  57 45 48 51 45 50 56 32 49 50 58 50 48 18”
 * @param string $sep               The separator
 * @return string
 */
function bytesToStr($bytes, $sep = ' ')
{
    $str = '';
    if (is_string($bytes)) {
        $bytes = explode($sep, $bytes);
    }
    foreach ($bytes as $ch) {
        $str .= chr($ch);
    }
    return $str;
}
```

