It seems like there is a problem with the unrolled unsafe loop in [CodedOutputStream#L1351-L1375](https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/blob/0a246e23f8e9997e2f7e5887b2523e867c8653c5/java/core/src/main/java/com/google/protobuf/CodedOutputStream.java#L1351-L1375).

Changing `position` to be a local variable makes the performance match the in-loop case (`290ns -> 40ns` for the int32s benchmark), i.e.,

```Java
int position = this.position;
try {
  // unrolled-loop
} finally {
  this.position = position;
}
```

There is probably an optimization that it's not picking up on. I haven't had a chance to look at the assembly or confirm it for other cases though.

