@shialex In proto3, a field will not serialize if it has the default value.  So, you can (temporarily) set fields that you don't want to serialize to be the default, do the serialization, and then restore.  

In your example above, if you set the phones field to be an empty list, then it won't serialize.

If you wanted to make this a general thing, then you could possibly use something like a google.protobuf.FieldMask, or other field specification, that could be used to suppress the serialization of unwanted fields.

