nodes.body:
For numeric types, the default value is zero. As far as I know, explicitly setting it to zero or not setting it at all, wouldn't make any difference when serializing the message. As the documentation regarding default values also mentions, if a scalar message field is set to its default value, the value will not be serialized.

https://developers.google.com/protocol-buffers/docs/proto3#default_values

This would in turn mean that the field won't show in the output you get when running `serializeToString()` if it has the default value. Later on the receiving end, when you parse the serialized message data (using for example `mergeFromString($data)` in PHP or  `ParseFromString(data)` in Python) and get the field value using the getter function on the object you'll end up with the default value again (in your case `0`).

```php

$from = new Test();
$from->setActive(0);

$data = $from->serializeToString();

$to = new Test();
$to->mergeFromString($data);

var_dump($to->getActive());
/* Output should be int(0) */
```

