The only way to reuse message fields in protobuf is to create a sub-message:

```
message Common {
  int64 id = 1;
  string category = 2;
}

message FirstMessage{
  Common common = 1;
  string description = 2;
  string name = 3;

  repeated int64 some_ids = 5;
}

message SecondMessage{
  Common common = 1;
  string description = 2;
  string name = 3;

  repeated string same_names = 5;
  string time_str = 6;
}
```

But the wire format for this is not compatible with your example.

Protobuf does not have message inheritance or any other feature that would let you "include" the same set of fields in two different messages.

