Protobuf message objects  in Python do not support reparenting. This means that the line:

```python
proto_wrapper_object = SyftNative(data_tensorproto_57=proto)
```

is actually copying the entire message tree from one message to another.

It so happens that these two protos are wire compatible with each other:

```
message SyftNative1 {
  bytes data = 1;
}

message SyftNative2 {
  <torch_tensor_proto> data_tensorproto_57 = 1;
}
```

So one option would be to serialize as `SyftNative1` when you want to wrap an existing message and then parse as `SyftNative2` on the other side.

This is a little bit tricky, but I think it might be your best option given the current APIs.

