  const newObj = {
    a: o.a,
  };
  
  if (o.someCondition) {
    newObj.b = someValue;
  }

  return newObj;
});
```

It's not as concise as other ways of writing a mapping function, but it works. I was able to skip setting the Protobuf message field when the source data's condition was met, causing the resulting Protobuf message to not have that field set (like my `Person` example where I don't set the field).

