@srth12 The results of `$message->serializeToJsonString()` will generally be very readable. You should see readable key/value pairs for all of your proto fields.

The only exception is for bytes fields, which will be encoded using base64. But bytes fields are not expected to be readable anyway.

I would encourage you to try `$message->serializeToJsonString()` on your protos. It should be very easy to try. You can see if you like the output. If you have any specific concerns about it, feel free to post a follow-up.

