code at wire_format_lite.h : 1429
inline uint8_t* WireFormatLite::WriteBoolNoTagToArray(bool value,
                                                      uint8_t* target) {
  return io::CodedOutputStream::WriteVarint32ToArray(value ? 1 : 0, target);
}

if value bigger than 128(0x80)，protobuf would write this number to the stream directly, and the ptr only moved by 1 byte.
It leads crash. 
The gcc compiler won't convert value to 0 or 1 in O2 optimize mode

this problem is hard to debug, I fixed it with:

inline uint8_t* WireFormatLite::WriteBoolNoTagToArray(bool value,
                                                      uint8_t* target) {
  if (value)
    return io::CodedOutputStream::WriteVarint32ToArray(1, target);
  else
    return io::CodedOutputStream::WriteVarint32ToArray(0, target);
  
}

