The discussion has been going on since [2008](https://groups.google.com/g/protobuf/c/UKpsthqAmjw). The main issue in using groups is the awful syntax, so why not promote `group` to be usable as a keyword similar to `message`?

```proto
message A {
  optional int32 a = 1;
}
group B {
   optional int32 b = 1;
}
message C {
  optional A a1 = 1;
  optional A a2 = 2;
  optional B b1 = 3;
  optional B b2 = 4;
}
```

which would result in the same encoding as the deprecated syntax

```proto
message A {
  optional int32 a = 1;
}
message C {
  optional A a1 = 1;
  optional A a2 = 2;
  optional group B1 = 3 {
     optional int32 b = 1;
  }
  optional group B2 = 4 {
     optional int32 b = 1;
  }
}
```

