Hey, I have a Python gRPC server with reflection enabled using the proto below. I'm trying to get information about the server from a C# client with the code below in GetServiceInformationAsync using FileDescriptor.BuildFromByteStrings, but it throws an exception: "Dependency missing: google/protobuf/timestamp.proto"

I've tried calling the alternative method signature that accepts an ExtensionRegistry, but couldn't figure out how to add WellKnownTypes.Timestamp to it so I don't know if that would solve the problem.

Is there another method I should be using to get the information I want from the RepeatedField\<ByteString\> that gRPC reflection provides me with? If not, how can I get it to include WellKnownTypes.Timestamp as a dependency when parsing?


Proto:
```proto
syntax = "proto3";
import "google/protobuf/timestamp.proto";

service Test {
  rpc ProcessData(Input) returns (Output);
}

message Input {
  google.protobuf.Timestamp DateTime = 1;
  double Value = 2;
}

message Output {
  google.protobuf.Timestamp DateTime = 1;
  double Value = 2;
}
```

C#:
```csharp
private static async Task GetServiceInformationAsync(GrpcChannel channel, string serviceName)
{
    var response = await ReflectionRequestAsync(
        channel,
        new ServerReflectionRequest
        {
            FileContainingSymbol = serviceName
        }
    );

    var descriptors = FileDescriptor.BuildFromByteStrings(
        response.FileDescriptorResponse.FileDescriptorProto
    );
}

private static async Task<ServerReflectionResponse> ReflectionRequestAsync(
    GrpcChannel channel,
    ServerReflectionRequest request
)
{
    var client = new ServerReflection.ServerReflectionClient(channel);
    using var stream = client.ServerReflectionInfo();

    await stream.RequestStream.WriteAsync(request);

    var value = await stream.ResponseStream.MoveNext(CancellationToken.None)
        ? stream.ResponseStream.Current
        : throw new EndOfStreamException();

    await stream.RequestStream.CompleteAsync();

    return value;
}
```

