Follow-up of #9658

This is important when passing messages that would be better represented as plain struct in C#, to avoid lots of allocations (e.g a `Point { float x, float y }` with a `repeated Point points` on it)

The idea is to support generating struct for message types by having an option on the message:

```
message MyMessage {
    option csharp_generate_struct = true;
    // fields...
}
```

The generated code for serialization/deserialization should generate optimal code using struct with by ref/in.

