Hmm, this is a somewhat strange corner case... this build is using Clang, but building against the MS STL. The MS toolchain (including the STL) always assumes some minimum C++ version, so forcing Clang to use C++11 is problematic when that minimum is above 11 (which it has been for ages now).

The reason we force C++11 is because the `check_cxx_source_compiles` function doesn't forward `CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD` and friends, so other platforms (notably, recent macOSes, but also older supported compilers) will fail due to an old language version.

