I think this is working as intended. In your example PositionGroup is not a subtype of Any or vice versa. Thus mergeFrom has the behavior expected of Any, not the mergeFrom behavior of PositionGroup. Thus there are no repeated fields to merge. any.proto only has two fields:

```
 string type_url = 1 [ctype = STRING_PIECE];
  bytes value = 2 [ctype = CORD];
 ```

Neither is repeated and both are merged here as expected. That is, Any is not java.lang.Object. When you store a proto message in an Any you lose all the type information and expected behavior of the original type. Protos are not self-describing.

