Okay, I've reproduced this.

The problem is in ParseContext.Initialize:

```csharp
internal static void Initialize(ReadOnlySpan<byte> buffer, out ParseContext ctx)
{
    ParserInternalState state = default;
    state.sizeLimit = DefaultSizeLimit;
    state.recursionLimit = DefaultRecursionLimit;
    state.currentLimit = int.MaxValue;
    state.bufferSize = buffer.Length;

    Initialize(buffer, ref state, out ctx);
}
```

The errors are:

> - This combination of arguments to 'ParseContext.Initialize(ReadOnlySpan<byte>, ref ParserInternalState, out ParseContext)' is disallowed because it may expose variables referenced by parameter 'state' outside of their declaration scope
> - Cannot return local 'state' by reference because it is not a ref local

I assume this fails in C# 11 due to more precise ref escape analysis.

The simplest fix for this is just to inline the initialization.

