I think you misunderstand, constructing `string_view(nullptr)` is indeed UB, because you don't specify length and it's treated as a C-string, computing length from that pointer. However, constructing `string_view(nullptr, 0)` should be totally fine, and default constructor is documented to have data as nullptr and size as 0:

https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view/basic_string_view

We parse serialized data into protobufs, and sometimes that data is empty. Also, we don't use strings, it's more like vectors. When empty they have data set to nullptr (I think the only reason string's data is never nullptr is because it's equivalent to c_str(), which must be nul-terminated). Let's say I do this:

```
std::vector<char> serialized;
google::protobuf::Empty msg;
msg.ParseFromArray(serialized.data(), serialized.size());
```

Do you think it should trigger ubsan? Currently it does.

