FYI our style guide recommends using lower_underscore case for field names (https://protobuf.dev/programming-guides/style/#message-field-names), so `_underscore` is not recommended and could hit other escaping problems.

The error is the result of escaping conflicting in proto3 synthetic oneofs by prepending with X in the parser for conflicts:
https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/blob/1856979d0e0ef825a338dfc6f4030dc0f8d95396/src/google/protobuf/compiler/parser.cc#L818

proto3 uses synthetic oneofs to represent proto3 optionals which results in conflicts for the FieldDescriptor's name (_underscore) and the OneofDescriptor's name (X_underscore since __underscore is reserved for cpp)

Oddly, double underscore seems to be allowed for **actual** oneofs. Maybe we may need to add escaping there too or can loosen this for synthetic oneofs if that comment is no longer current. The following proto results in FieldDescriptor with _oneof and OneofDescriptor __oneof, which is similar to the `optional string _underscore` case.
```
message Proto3Break {
  oneof __oneof {
    string _oneof = 1;
  }
}
```

In any case, I believe we can probably handle the X_ escaping here by adding special handling for synthetic oneofs with FieldDescriptors for clear (like with has/get/etc) in https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/blob/1856979d0e0ef825a338dfc6f4030dc0f8d95396/java/core/src/main/java/com/google/protobuf/GeneratedMessageV3.java#L2251

