Your friends may be using `syntax = "proto2";` or they may be using proto3 + optional fields.

If you specify your field as optional (in proto2 or proto3), even the default 0 value will get serialized:
```
syntax = "proto3";
package abc;
message Status {

  optional StatusCodeType statusCode = 1;

  enum StatusCodeType {
    SUCCESS = 0;
    ERROR = 1;
  }
}
```

*Best Practices Note:* If you want to stick with "implicit" presence, which is the default in proto3, we recommend that you use the 0 enum value for a placeholder value named `STATUS_CODE_UNSPECIFIED`.

To learn more about field presence read here:
