nodes.body:
@jeena1030 
`oneof` is not allowed to contain a `repeated` field.

The most common solution is to make a wrapper message for your repeated field.

In this case with these generic field names:
```
message Int32List {
  repeated int32 value = 1;
}
message DoubleList {
  repeated double value = 1;
}
message Data {
  int64 id = 1;
  oneof value {
    int32 int_value = 2;
    double double_value = 3;
    string string_value = 4;
    Int32List int32 int_array_value = 5;
    DoubleList repeated double double_array_value = 6;
  }
  int32 area = 7;
}
```

Note that it is tempting to create a generic list wrapper type for the primitive values like `Int32List` and reuse it in multiple situations. That can lead to confusion about the sensitivity of data in fields using that list type. In general, I would recommend creating list wrapper messages with *specific* names and documentation for the data contained there.

Creating wrapper messages like this is a pattern that can also be used if you need to detect that a repeated field is "present and empty" or "not present at all" which cannot be distinguished in the direct repeated field case.

