@gregoryfm - Can you clarify what gem you're using that has an explicit dependency on 3.23.4? That version is no longer supported (see https://protobuf.dev/support/version-support/#ruby-support for documentation on what versions are currently maintained).

If you need a protobuf version that targets a higher Ruby interpreter version, you'll need to use a later release, preferably the latest.

My educated guess is that because https://rubygems.org/gems/google-protobuf/versions/3.23.4 is a source gem, it may be possible for end users to use it to build against arbitrary Ruby interpreter versions, whereas https://rubygems.org/gems/google-protobuf/versions/3.23.4-x86_64-linux is a precompiled version build against a Ruby interpreter prior to the release of Ruby 3.3 and therefore may not have binary compatibility.

